{"complete":true,"city":"Medina, Saudi Arabia","template_id":"global-first-24-hours","title":"Your First 24 Hours in Medina, Dealt as Cards","description":"A ten-stop first day that begins at Medina’s spiritual center, reads the city through prayer grounds, museums and battle landscapes, pauses over regional cooking, and closes at Quba.","icon":"schedule","cards":[{"entity_name":"The Prophet’s Mosque","title":"The Prophet’s Mosque","subtitle":"Daybreak anchor","notes":"Begin quietly in the mosque and its courtyards. This is a place of worship associated with the Prophet’s life and companions, so let prayer and local etiquette set the pace.","short_summary":"Start where the Prophet built his mosque after arriving in Medina; later expansions have carried the complex through successive eras.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/The-Prophet%27s-Mosque","source_title":"The Prophet's Mosque | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"The Prophet’s Mosque Museum","title":"The Prophet’s Mosque Museum","subtitle":"Read the building","notes":"Use the models and multilingual presentations to decode the pulpit, mihrab, domes, gates and successive expansions before encountering those elements elsewhere.","short_summary":"The museum documents more than 1,400 years of the mosque’s architecture through visual, written and audio material.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/The-Prophet%27s-Mosque-Museum","source_title":"The Prophet's Mosque Museum | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Al-Ghamamah Mosque","title":"Al-Ghamamah Mosque","subtitle":"Trace the old prayer ground","notes":"Notice the basalt, white lime and sequence of domes. The structure marks part of Al-Musalla, where the Prophet led Eid and rain-invoking prayers.","short_summary":"This mosque preserves one of the prayer sites in the former open ground southwest of the Prophet’s Mosque.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/Al-Ghamamah-Mosque","source_title":"Al-Ghamamah Mosque | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Chefs Market","title":"Chefs Market","subtitle":"First substantial meal","notes":"Choose by appetite rather than trying to survey every counter. The documented range includes mandi, madhbi, kebab, Kabuli and Bukhari rice, manto and yaghmush.","short_summary":"A long-established food complex brings numerous traditional restaurants and cuisines from across the Islamic world into one market.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/Chefs-Market","source_title":"Chefs Market | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Al-Qiblatain Mosque","title":"Al-Qiblatain Mosque","subtitle":"Locate a turning point","notes":"Give this stop one focused question: how does a building hold the memory of a changed direction? The mosque commemorates the shift of the qibla toward the Kaaba.","short_summary":"Its name and identity are tied to the 2 AH event in which the direction of Muslim prayer changed from Jerusalem to Mecca.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/Al-Qiblatain-Mosque","source_title":"Al-Qiblatain Mosque | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"The Seven Mosques","title":"The Seven Mosques","subtitle":"Read the trench landscape","notes":"Look beyond the collective name: the official account explains that five small historic mosques remain here and that the label “Seven Mosques” developed later.","short_summary":"The group stands at the foot of Mount Sila’, near the setting of the Battle of the Trench.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/The-Seven-Mosques","source_title":"The Seven Mosques | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Uhud Martyrs Square","title":"Uhud Martyrs Square","subtitle":"Set the battle in terrain","notes":"Use Mount Uhud, Archers’ Hill and the martyrs’ cemetery as three reference points. The terrain makes the official account of the battle’s changing course easier to follow.","short_summary":"The square gathers major landmarks associated with the Battle of Uhud, including the mountain, Archers’ Hill and the cemetery of the martyrs.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/Uhud-Martyrs-Square","source_title":"Uhud Martyrs Square | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Dar Al-Madinah Museum","title":"Dar Al-Madinah Museum","subtitle":"Reassemble the city","notes":"Shift from outdoor sites to models, photographs, manuscripts and architectural material. The exhibits connect the Prophet’s biography with Medina’s changing urban form.","short_summary":"The museum preserves Medina’s Islamic and architectural heritage through dedicated halls, models, images and historical collections.","source_url":"https://www.visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/Dar-Al-Madinah-museum-","source_title":"Dar Al-Madinah museum | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Hijaz Railway Museum","title":"Hijaz Railway Museum","subtitle":"Add the rail-era layer","notes":"Study the surviving station buildings and railway material as evidence of how pilgrims once entered Medina from Damascus and points farther north.","short_summary":"The restored terminal station now presents the Hijaz Railway alongside galleries covering Medina from the pre-Islamic period to the modern era.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/Hijaz-Railway-Museum","source_title":"Hijaz Railway Museum | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null},{"entity_name":"Quba Mosque","title":"Quba Mosque","subtitle":"Close with the migration story","notes":"End with worship or quiet observation. Quba returns the day to the Prophet’s arrival in Medina and the foundation of the first mosque in Islam.","short_summary":"The mosque was founded after the Prophet’s migration and remains connected to the Prophet’s Mosque by the Quba walking trail.","source_url":"https://visitmadinahsa.com/sa-en/destinations/Quba-Mosque","source_title":"Quba Mosque | Madinah","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"place_id":null,"maps_url":null}],"warnings":["The supplied input contained no candidate places. Accordingly, every place_id, maps_url and coordinate field is null."]}
